  39:     - The dominant background color forms complete separator rows and columns,
  40:       including the outer border.
  41:     - The separator lines divide the foreground into a rectangular lattice of
  42:       same-sized filled blocks.
  43:     - Every block has one unique majority color and contains no background cells.
  44: 
  45:     Rule
  46:     - Find the contiguous non-separator row bands and column bands.
  47:     - For each band intersection, write the unique majority color of that input
  48:       block to the corresponding interior cell of the output.
  49:     - Leave a one-cell background border around the summarized lattice.
